  "output": "The pipe seems to be getting mangled by this shell. Let me verify how pipes behave here.Confirmed — this environment passes `|` through literally instead of interpreting it. I can work around that by wrapping the pipeline in `sh -c`:Done. Since this environment doesn't interpret `|` directly (it gets passed through literally), I wrapped the pipeline in `sh -c`. The single piped command and its output:\n\n```sh\nls projects/wiki | grep -E 'i18n|locale|translation'\n```\n\nResult:\n```\ni18n.json\nlocale.md\ntranslation.yml\n```\n\n`readme.txt` is correctly filtered out, since its name matches none of the three patterns.",
